  "scopeLimits": [
    "Only POST /users changed. Membership commands, other handlers, schemas, shared helpers, policies and migrations are unchanged.",
    "Administrators by legacy flag and by global binding enroll through real HTTP/TOTP in the same session family. No positive MFA proof is fabricated by SQL.",
    "Baseline has six201 and four409 versus403 failures, with complete preceding data/audit/password or unchanged-duplicate diagnostics. Duplicate outcomes do not prove an unauthorized write.",
    "Two narrowly scoped AFTER INSERT triggers (users/audit_logs) execute once each; fixed rollback restores users, audits and exact original proof timestamp text/generation/presence.",
    "Positive cases retain the seven-field public DTO, defaults and rich values, hashed password, new-account HTTP login, platform audit, duplicate inactive accounts, validation, recent password reauthentication and authority restrictions.",
    "Global binding withdrawal after real authorization preserves capability refusal. This test observes an interleaving, not an actual PostgreSQL lock wait.",
    "V1 had thirteen failures from incorrect header expectations and four409/403 mismatches. V2 removes only three Cache-Control assertions; product and all MFA/data/audit assertions stay identical. Cache policy is not accepted by this batch.",
    "The initial low-memory refusal is preserved. The later preparations/types/runs used the unchanged1536MiB guard; other projects were not stopped by this task.",
    "Fourteen related regression files retain their own limits. Historical runs and baseline are not added to corrected counts.",
    "Membership/support/features commands, other domains, generic trigger exceptions, promotion and actual lock waits remain outside this acceptance.",
    "No browser, native Android/iOS, full API, performance, universal commit-boundary guarantee or production acceptance is asserted."
  ],
